The two dlib models this project downloads at build time are not covered by the
licence above and are not redistributed here:

  shape_predictor_68_face_landmarks.dat
      Derived from the iBUG 300-W dataset. Licensed for research purposes only;
      commercial use requires a licence from Imperial College London.
      https://github.com/davisking/dlib-models

  dlib_face_recognition_resnet_model_v1.dat
      CC0 / public domain, per its author.
      https://github.com/davisking/dlib-models

The detector weights (models/best.pt, models/best.onnx) were trained with
Ultralytics YOLOv8, which is AGPL-3.0. Ultralytics takes the position that this
extends to models trained with it and to software that serves them. That reading
is contested and this note is not legal advice, but if you intend to use these
weights commercially, resolve it first -- either by obtaining an Ultralytics
Enterprise licence or by retraining the detector on a permissively licensed
implementation. Nothing about the MIT grant above changes the terms attached to
the weights.
